# Scrubbing while paused: SetTime is a one-way, latest-wins latch slot. The
# frame shows in the next Frame header at once; Time at Rest is committed
# with one debounced ProjectSnapshot once no SetTime has arrived for 250 ms
# and the frame differs from the last committed one. A SetTime naming a shot
# other than the active one is logged and ignored.

connect
set-encodings raw
set-frame-config 32 24
start-rendering
await-frame
assert shot.active.playing == false
assert frame.frame == 0

# Two scrubs back to back: the later one wins; a frame at 7 arrives.
set-time active 3
set-time active 7
await-frame-at 7

# The debounced rest snapshot: one, for the frame the scrub ended on.
await-snapshot
assert shot.active.currentFrame == 7
assert snapshots.received == 2

# Not the active shot: no frame moves, no snapshot follows, no Error either.
set-time shot_9999 9
sleep 500
assert snapshots.received == 2
assert frame.frame == 7
assert errors.received == 0

# Scrubbing to the frame already committed changes nothing to commit.
set-time active 7
sleep 500
assert snapshots.received == 2

# And a scrub elsewhere commits again.
set-time active 2
await-frame-at 2
await-snapshot
assert shot.active.currentFrame == 2
assert snapshots.received == 3

stop-rendering
disconnect
